modules=[
 ('0 · AI Literacy','5/10','One agentic lesson is a useful introduction; fix exaggerated quality claims. Add scope selection, source inspection and approval judgment. Reflection alone does not demonstrate those skills.'),
 ('1 · Foundations','6/10','Chat-specific create/run exercise and SearchSet credit exist. Lessons still send the learner into a workflow editor. Grade the actual lab extraction and source-checked values.'),
 ('2 · Thinking in Workflows','4/10','Process decomposition remains valuable. Add a decision between a one-off chat task, a project, a saved extraction/workflow and automation. Assess an applied choice.'),
 ('3 · Workflow Design','6/10','A dedicated chat design lesson exists. Require the learner to identify and repair a bad proposed plan, approve the right scope and choose a human checkpoint.'),
 ('4 · Extraction Engine','5/10','Chat proposing and guided verification appear in exercise steps. The count-based grader does not enforce the promised accuracy or field-configuration criteria.'),
 ('5 · Multi-Step Workflows','5/10','The exercise can be authored/run from chat. Add approval review, inspection of actual step outputs, and recovery without repeating successful writes.'),
 ('6 · Advanced Nodes','3/10','The exercise is mostly the existing node/parallelism lesson wrapped in chat. Fix the arithmetic guidance; teach tool boundaries and safe handling of unavailable capabilities.'),
 ('7 · Output & Delivery','4/10','Editor handoff is a valid precision workflow, but it should be explicit and return cleanly to chat. Require opening and checking the actual delivered file from the same run.'),
 ('8 · Validation & QA','7/10','Strongest update: trust tiers and guided verification are dedicated lessons. Add Unscored/stale/critical cases and require explaining a failing or regressed result.'),
 ('9 · Batch Processing','5/10','Chat extraction on multiple documents counts. Teach document scope, partial failure and retry in chat; verify the intended batch and sampled source values.'),
 ('10 · Governance','4/10','Sharing/examiner concepts have useful updated language; submission-based completion avoids waiting on an examiner. Missing assessed project/team scope, data boundaries, automation approvals and artifact ownership.'),
]
